[
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there some way to automatically derive \"easy\" <code>Decidable</code> instances like the following?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isNice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- deriving DecidablePred</span>\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> Failed to delta derive `Decidable` instance for `isNice`, the class has no explicit non-out-param parameters where</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  x✝.isNice</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">can be inserted. -/</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DecidablePred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isNice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_|_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isNice</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instDecidableFalse</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instDecidableTrue</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 603133372,
        "sender_full_name": "Malvin Gattinger",
        "timestamp": 1781469682
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>what about defining the function in question as a mapping to <code>Bool</code> instead of <code>Prop</code>?</p>",
        "id": 603147745,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1781475314
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hm, that works and seems the obvious solution in my MWE above. But in a larger project it also makes proofs uglier with <code>... = true</code> added.</p>\n<p>To rephrase my question: in which cases does <code>deriving DecidablePred</code> ever work? And where can I read more about what \"delta deriving\" means?</p>",
        "id": 603255476,
        "sender_full_name": "Malvin Gattinger",
        "timestamp": 1781508958
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If anything, you probably want to derive <code>Decidable</code> (<code>DecidablePred</code> is just an abbrev for <code>Decidable</code>). Then it should work exactly if you can derive <code>Decidable</code> for the body:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span>\n<span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Decidable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- we can synthesize Decidable for the body</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isNice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>\n<span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Decidable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- so it works</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The problem for your example is that there is no <code>Decidable</code> instance for the match expression.</p>",
        "id": 603429915,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1781541353
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, thanks. Is there any way to get/derive <code>Decidable</code> instances for match expressions? Or is that something fundamentally not possible / hard to do?</p>",
        "id": 603479591,
        "sender_full_name": "Malvin Gattinger",
        "timestamp": 1781551886
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well you can certainly write a macro that does something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"derive_decide_split_for \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Decidable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">id</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dsimp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">repeat'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">split</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">infer_instance</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isNice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">derive_decide_split_for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bla</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isNice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but just with regular <code>deriving Decidable</code>, you have the limitations of instance synthesis and there just simply isn't a theorem for <code>Decidable</code> with a match statement (and no other mechanism in instance synthesis that would make this work).</p>",
        "id": 603484913,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1781553177
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>just want to add that Lean has a coercion from <code>Bool</code> to <code>Prop</code>, so in many (most?) cases you don't need to explicitly write <code>... = true</code> if you're working with a boolean function in <code>Prop</code> contexts (though it's true that Lean will display it in the InfoView as <code>... = true</code>)</p>",
        "id": 603490365,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1781554497
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"+1\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f44d\" role=\"img\" title=\"+1\">:+1:</span> for the \"where can I read more about what delta deriving means\"</p>",
        "id": 603523339,
        "sender_full_name": "Filippo A. E. Nuccio",
        "timestamp": 1781563926
    }
]